  "id": "7740f16223ddea4c3ab1009f",
  "title": "datasette-charts 0.2a0",
  "summary": "Release: datasette-charts 0.2a0 I introduced this new charting plugin for Datasette yesterday . Today it's gained integration with Datasette Agent , so now you can ask chat for a chart and it will create one for you using the same underlying chart suggestion and generation tools. Here's a demo video, recorded on agent.datasette.io where you can sign in with…",
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-charts/releases/tag/0.2a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette-charts 0.2a0</a></p>\n        <p>I introduced this new charting plugin for Datasette <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/23/datasette-charts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">yesterday</a>. Today it&#x27;s gained integration with <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Datasette Agent</a>, so now you can ask chat for a chart and it will create one for you using the same underlying chart suggestion and generation tools.</p>\n<p>Here&#x27;s a demo video, recorded on <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">agent.datasette.io</a>  where you can sign in with GitHub to try the plugin yourself:</p>\n<figure>\n  \n    \n    <a href=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-charts-agent-demo.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the video (MP4)</a>\n  \n  <figcaption>\n    I prompt Datasette Agent to &quot;Use #stats to show sqlite-utils downloads over time as a chart&quot; - where typing &quot;#stats&quot; opens a table search box. It shows me a chart inline in the chat, and when I click &quot;Open in the chart builder&quot; it opens the chart in a panel along with the table page. I use the table page to switch to a chart of &quot;datasette&quot;, then when I ask the agent &quot;what does the chart show?&quot; it notices that I changed the content in the panel and describes the new Datasette chart to me.\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>\n\n<p>Here&#x27;s <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/simonw/12646fcc72dddae3d4ac04b496c20af2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">a Markdown export</a> of the chat from the video.</p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette-agent</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/visualization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">visualization</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-charts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette-charts</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/sqlite\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sqlite</a></p>",
